---
/**
 * /design, the tokens: surfaces and accents painted from `var(--name)`, their
 * values read back from the live stylesheet by the page script, and a real
 * capture's palette row.
 */
import PaletteRow from "../PaletteRow.astro";
import { sites } from "../../lib/sites";

/**
 * The surface tokens, by name only.
 *
 * No values here. A value typed into this file would be the copy the page
 * exists to not have: the swatch is painted `var(--name)` and the string beside
 * it is read out of the live stylesheet on load, so both halves answer to
 * `styles/global.css` and to whichever theme the reader is in.
 */
const SURFACES = [
  { name: "--bg", note: "the page" },
  { name: "--text-primary", note: "titles, long-form prose, and the mark" },
  { name: "--text-secondary", note: "standfirsts, controls, and every paragraph on this page" },
  { name: "--text-tertiary", note: "metadata: dates, counts, labels" },
  { name: "--text-quaternary", note: "decoration only: the crumb divider" },
  { name: "--surface-2", note: "a raised surface" },
  { name: "--surface-3", note: "a deeper one: code, the menu's hover" },
  { name: "--surface-selected", note: "the selected row in a list" },
  { name: "--hairline", note: "every border on the site" },
  { name: "--hairline-strong", note: "a hovered row border, a swatch edge" },
  { name: "--outline", note: "the 1px inset on imagery" },
  { name: "--dot", note: "the dotted grid behind a framed screenshot" },
];

/** The accent, and the pair that exists because white on it fails AA. */
const ACCENTS = [
  { name: "--accent", note: "ink only: links, hover, aria-current, focus" },
  { name: "--accent-panel", note: "the accent as a background with text on it" },
  { name: "--accent-panel-ink", note: "that text" },
  { name: "--amber-ink", note: "the second accent: the on-hold pill's word" },
  { name: "--amber-bg", note: "the pill behind it" },
  { name: "--highlight", note: "a highlighter mark behind words" },
  { name: "--selection-bg", note: "selected text: blue in light, orange in dark" },
];

/** The newest capture in the gallery, so the palette row below is a real one. */
const capture = sites[0]!;
---

<section>
  <h2 class="sheet__head mono">Tokens</h2>
  <p>
    Every colour on the site is one of these. Light is the base. Dark is
    written twice: once for a reader following their OS, once for a reader
    who pinned it.
  </p>
  <p>
    The values beside the swatches are read from the live stylesheet, so
    they follow the theme button in the footer. They&rsquo;re the shipped
    strings, so the minifier has shortened some hexes to three digits and
    folded alpha in where it could.
  </p>

  <ul class="tokens">
    {
      SURFACES.map((token) => (
        <li class="tok">
          <span
            class="tok__chip"
            style={`background: var(${token.name})`}
            aria-hidden="true"
          />
          <span class="tok__head">
            <span class="code">{token.name}</span>
            <span class="code tok__value" data-token={token.name}>
              ----
            </span>
          </span>
          <span class="tok__note">{token.note}</span>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ul>

  <p>
    The accent is one hue at two lightnesses. The hue is identical in both
    themes and lightness is the only difference, because no single lightness
    clears 4.5:1 against both a white page and a near-black one. Amber is
    the second accent. It marks things and is never a link.
  </p>

  <ul class="tokens">
    {
      ACCENTS.map((token) => (
        <li class="tok">
          <span
            class="tok__chip"
            style={`background: var(${token.name})`}
            aria-hidden="true"
          />
          <span class="tok__head">
            <span class="code">{token.name}</span>
            <span class="code tok__value" data-token={token.name}>
              ----
            </span>
          </span>
          <span class="tok__note">{token.note}</span>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ul>

  <p class="panel">
    The moment the accent becomes a background with text on it, it switches
    to the panel pair. White on the dark theme's accent is 3.89:1 and fails
    AA; white on this blue is 5.91:1 in either theme, which is why this block
    is the same blue whichever theme you are reading it in.
  </p>

  <p>
    The palette row that sits under every screenshot in the gallery. Every
    swatch is a button that copies its hex. These six were measured off the <a
    href={`/sites/${capture.slug}`}>{capture.title}</a> screenshot.
  </p>

  <div class="capture">
    <PaletteRow palette={capture.palette} title={capture.title} />
  </div>
</section>

<style>

  /* --- tokens ----------------------------------------------------------- */

  .tokens {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }


  .tok {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2.75rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 0.15rem 0.9rem;
    align-items: center;
    padding-block: 0.7rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }


  .tok__chip {
    grid-row: span 2;
    align-self: center;
    width: 2.75rem;
    height: 2.75rem;
    /* Sharp, like every other swatch on the site: a 4px corner marks a token you
       could pick up, and this is a surface you look at. Inset, so a --bg swatch
       on a light page is a chip rather than a hole, and so the eight-percent
       tokens below are visible at all. */
    border-radius: 0;
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--hairline-strong);
  }


  .tok__head {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 0.25rem 1rem;
  }


  .tok__head .code:first-child {
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }


  .tok__note {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
  }


  /* Held at the vivid blue in both themes, which is the point it is making. */
  .panel {
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.15rem;
    background: var(--accent-panel);
  }


  .capture {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }
</style>
